  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A solid sphere of radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\"></span> and mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> is released from rest and rolls down a slope, without slipping. The vertical height of the slope is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"h\"></span>. The moment of inertia <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span> of this sphere about an axis through its centre is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2}{5}mr^{2}\"></span>.</p><p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p><p>Show that the linear velocity <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span> of the sphere as it leaves the slope is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{\\frac{10gh}{7}}\"></span>.</p><p>[3]</p>"
